{"text": "# Case management notes — Tidewater Home Health & Hospice\n\n**Client:** Adaeze Okonkwo-Bell (\"Miss Addie\") · **DOB:** Jan. 4, 1930 · **Age:** 96\n**Client ID:** THH-26-00418 · **MBI:** 4EG7-TK5-MW93 · **Cert period:** 09/14/2026 – 11/12/2026\n**RN case manager:** Tamsin Reyes, RN · **HHA:** Luis Carrasquillo\n**PCP:** Dr. Imogen Faircloth, Faircloth Internal Medicine, 757-555-0112\n\n## Home & access\n\n- 614 Poplar Hall Lane, Norfolk, VA 23502. Single-story brick; ramp at side door.\n- Lockbox on side door, code **1930**. Alarm panel code 40418#. Do **not** give either to vendors.\n- Daughter and POA: Ngozi Bell-Hampton, lives in Raleigh, cell 919 555 0144, ngozi.bh@familymail.example. Calls every evening at 7.\n- Neighbor \"Hank\" at 618 has a key and checks the mail.\n- Family care portal: https://family.tidewaterhh.example/c/THH-26-00418 — daughter's login is nbellhampton.\n\n## Diagnoses / meds (from Form CMS-485)\n\n| Problem | Notes |\n|---|---|\n| Alzheimer's dementia, moderate | MoCA 14/30 in August |\n| CHF, EF 35% | furosemide 40 mg daily; daily weights |\n| COPD on home O2 2 L | concentrator serial OC5-2291-447A |\n| Type 2 DM | glipizide 5 mg with breakfast |\n| Recent fall | R hip contusion, no fx, ED visit 10/02/2026 |\n\nAlso PRN lorazepam 0.5 mg at bedtime for sundowning — daughter keeps it locked up.\n\n## Visit notes\n\n**10/06/2026 (TR)** — Start-of-care reassessment after the fall, OASIS-E completed. Weight 131, up 4 lb in a week; ankles 2+. Called Dr. Faircloth's office, new order: furosemide 40 mg twice daily x 3 days, then recheck. Client oriented to self only. She asked several times for \"Emeka,\" her late husband. PT/OT evals ordered. Medical alert pendant from AllHours Medical Alert was in a drawer; device ID AH-PND-0091447. Put it back on her and tested it.\n\n**10/09/2026 (LC)** — Bath and breakfast. Ate about half. She would not let me in at first; thought I was \"the man from the bank.\" Found three envelopes of cash in the bread box, about $2,300 total. Told Ms. Bell-Hampton by phone, who says her brother in Lagos sometimes asks their mother to wire money and she wants that stopped.\n\n**10/13/2026 (TR)** — Weight 127. Lungs clearer. Sat 93% on 2 L. Chesapeake Senior Meals delivery restarted (5 lunches/wk, client pays $3.50 a meal). Discussed with Ngozi that Medicare Part A home health will not cover 24-hour care; she is pricing private aides at $31/hr and thinks the family can manage about 4k a month. Client is a retired Navy civilian nurse; daughter will look into survivor benefits. Hospice not appropriate yet but explained the benefit.\n\n**10/16/2026 (LC)** — Miss Addie in good spirits, sang along to the radio. BP 138/70. No new bruises. Hank's truck (VA plate XKC-4471) was blocking the ramp again; left a note.\n\n## To do\n\n- [ ] Recert visit due by 11/10/2026\n- [ ] Ask Dr. Faircloth about a palliative consult\n- [ ] Wi-Fi for the telehealth tablet: network \"BellHouse\", password magnolia1930; tablet serial TB8-X447-1182\n- [ ] Advance directive on file (DNR signed 2024); copy to fridge folder", "kind": "Markdown document", "detail": "510 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Adaeze Okonkwo-Bell", "Luis Carrasquillo", "Tamsin Reyes", "Imogen Faircloth", "Ngozi Bell-Hampton", "Emeka", "Miss Addie", "Hank"], "companies": ["Tidewater Home Health & Hospice", "Faircloth Internal Medicine", "Familymail", "AllHours Medical Alert", "Medicare"]}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.09999999776482582, "modelMs": 28095.599999997765, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "phone", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "street", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "names"], "detections": [{"start": 26, "end": 57, "text": "Tidewater Home Health & Hospice", "kind": "company", "source": "model", "canonical": "Tidewater Home Health & Hospice"}, {"